-- title:
--   Image of the ∞-component is the closure of its generic point
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of the structure `DRModelPackage p` (a bundle of data and properties for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` $=$ `TwoChartIntegralModel ℤ (modularFunctionFieldFull p) (IgusaScheme.jFull p)` over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$, among them the component morphism `compInf` and the curve `ratModel` used below), let $O$ be a local ring whose maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism. Consider the composite of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathtt{compInf}\,\kappa$, which maps the scheme $(\mathfrak{X}.\mathtt{ratModel}\,\kappa).C$ into the base change $\mathfrak{X}_\kappa = \operatorname{DRModel}(p) \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}} \operatorname{Spec}\kappa$, followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`, the morphism $\mathfrak{X}_\kappa \to \mathfrak{X}_O$ obtained from the identity on $\operatorname{DRModel}(p)$ and $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$ on the base. The assertion is that the set-theoretic image of the underlying continuous map of this composite is exactly the topological closure of the single point which is the image of the generic point of $(\mathfrak{X}.\mathtt{ratModel}\,\kappa).C$, and that this image is a closed subset of $\mathfrak{X}_O$.
--
--   This identifies the image in the base change $\mathfrak{X}_O$ of one distinguished component of the geometric special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model as the irreducible closed subset cut out by the image of its generic point. It is used in the local analysis of the special fibre at the crossing points, for instance by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_maximalIdeal_eq_branchIdeal_sup_span_singleton`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_maximalIdeal_eq_branchIdeal_sup_span_singleton), [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_stalk_mul_eq_baseGerm_pow_and_isUnit_stalkSpecializes_of_crossing`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_stalk_mul_eq_baseGerm_pow_and_isUnit_stalkSpecializes_of_crossing) and [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart).
-- source:
